{
  "about": "Shared case table for the structural blank-slide predicates (#314 follow-up, plan D4 + PLAN-CORRECTIONS C4). Read by tests/unit/test_deck_spec_slides.py (Python: is_blank_slide_html, is_blank_slide_spec) and by Task 7's frontend/src/services/__tests__/blankSlide.test.ts (isBlankSlideHtml, isBlankSlideSpec). Rules, both languages: text is blank iff, after dropping comments, it holds only HTML ASCII whitespace [\\t\\n\\f\\r ]; the 'slide' class token match is case-sensitive; the first .slide (the end of the chain) must itself be a <div> (has_slide_wrapper / SLIDE_DIV_PATTERN are regexes over the raw string, so a <div class=slide> inside a comment or an attribute value satisfies them: check the element, e.g. localName === 'div') (TS: classList.contains, never querySelector: DOMParser text/html without a doctype is quirks mode, where .slide matches class=Slide). DOMParser hoists head-only elements that come BEFORE the root (style, meta, link, title, script, base) into <head>, and a leading comment onto the Document: the TS walk must count anything in <head> as off-chain. Do not add rows that the two parsers build into different trees (block elements inside <p>, tables, CDATA).",
